.TH "CADDY-VALIDATE" "1" "August 2021"
.SH NAME
.HP
caddy-validate \- Tests whether a configuration file is valid
.SH SYNOPSIS
.HP
caddy validate --config <path> [--adapter <name>]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP 
Loads and provisions the provided config, but does not start running it.
This reveals any errors with the configuration through the loading and
provisioning stages.
.SH OPTIONS
.HP
\fB-adapter\fR <string>
.RS
Name of config adapter
.RE 
.HP
\fB-config\fR <string>
.RS
Input configuration file
.RE  
.SH SEE ALSO
caddy-adapt(1), caddy-environ(1), caddy-file-server(1), caddy-fmt(1), caddy-hash-password(1), caddy-help(1), caddy-list-modules(1), caddy-reload(1), caddy-reverse-proxy(1), caddy-run(1), caddy-start(1), caddy-stop(1), caddy-trust(1), caddy-untrust(1)
